; Deliberately empty of settings. Read this before adding one.
;
; Do NOT add `legacy-peer-deps=true`. It sat here until 2026-11-06 and makes npm
; ignore peerDependencies entirely: a conflicting peer produces no warning, and
; `--strict-peer-deps` does not override it. While it was on, the tree drifted
; into two peer conflicts nobody saw (react-dom vs apps/mobile's exact react pin,
; and @astrojs/tailwind vs astro 7), and a wrong peer range upstream
; (@antiphony/capture-kit 0.2.0's `react: ^19.3.1`) installed silently.
;
; If you hit a peer conflict you cannot resolve, use `overrides` in the root
; package.json for that ONE package, with a `//overrides.<pkg>` note saying why:
; narrow, visible in a diff, and it does not switch off peer resolution for the
; whole tree.
